WEBVTT

00:12.120 --> 00:14.800
[Ada] My brother apologises
for not being here

00:14.880 --> 00:17.480
and would like to invite all of you
to his home for a meeting.

00:17.560 --> 00:19.960
[Tommy] All you have to do
is sit with Jack Nelson

00:20.040 --> 00:22.040
and talk to him about a new golden age.

00:22.120 --> 00:24.880
-If anyone's going to kill Tommy Shelby--
-It will be you.

00:24.960 --> 00:26.760
The future belongs to us.

00:26.840 --> 00:28.280
Your daughter has consumption.

00:28.360 --> 00:30.720
Consumption is a very infectious disease.

00:30.800 --> 00:32.840
[Lizzie] While they are X-raying Ruby,
they have to X-ray us.

00:32.920 --> 00:34.760
It's the girl's mother who laid the curse.

00:34.840 --> 00:36.960
Perhaps she waited
till your little girl was seven.

00:37.040 --> 00:38.400
So you'd know how it feels.

00:38.480 --> 00:40.920
[Tommy] Now that I'm without whiskey,
I can hear the spirits clearly,

00:41.000 --> 00:43.360
they are saying Ruby will be well
if I make amends.

00:43.440 --> 00:44.480
She's gone, Tommy.

00:51.200 --> 00:53.200
[latch clanks]

01:06.760 --> 01:08.760
["In This Heart" playing]

01:08.840 --> 01:12.520
[woman] ♪ In this heart ♪

01:12.600 --> 01:19.200
♪ Lies for you ♪

01:19.840 --> 01:22.200
♪ A lark ♪

01:22.280 --> 01:28.040
♪ Born only for you ♪

01:28.880 --> 01:31.560
♪ Who sings ♪

01:31.640 --> 01:36.920
♪ Only to you ♪

01:37.560 --> 01:44.560
♪ My love, my love, my love ♪

01:46.160 --> 01:52.280
-[woman] ♪ I am waiting ♪
-[man] ♪ Waiting ♪

01:52.360 --> 01:57.080
-[woman] ♪ For you ♪
-[man] ♪ For you ♪

01:57.960 --> 02:03.600
-[woman] ♪ For only ♪
-[man] ♪ For only ♪

02:03.680 --> 02:06.680
-[woman] ♪ To adore you ♪
-[man] ♪ To adore you ♪

02:06.760 --> 02:11.440
-[woman] ♪ My heart is for you ♪
-[man] ♪ My heart is for you ♪

02:11.960 --> 02:18.920
-[woman] ♪ My love, my love, my love ♪
-[man] ♪ My love, my love, my love ♪

02:21.280 --> 02:26.800
-[woman] ♪ This is my grief ♪
-[man] ♪ This is my grief ♪

02:27.600 --> 02:32.360
-[woman] ♪ For you ♪
-[man] ♪ For you ♪

02:33.600 --> 02:39.680
-[woman] ♪ I will have you ♪
-[man] ♪ I will have you ♪

02:39.760 --> 02:44.160
-[woman] ♪ With me ♪
-[man] ♪ With me ♪

02:45.560 --> 02:52.520
-[woman] ♪ In my arms only ♪
-[man] ♪ In my arms only ♪

02:55.080 --> 03:00.840
-[woman] ♪ For you are only ♪
-[man] ♪ For you are only ♪

03:01.560 --> 03:06.800
-[woman] ♪ My love, my love ♪
-[man] ♪ My love, my love ♪

03:07.760 --> 03:13.400
-[woman] ♪ My love ♪
-[man] ♪ My love ♪

03:36.160 --> 03:37.200
Arthur.

03:40.000 --> 03:41.400
I've written some words.

03:43.400 --> 03:44.640
I can't speak 'em.

03:46.000 --> 03:46.880
[grunts]

03:46.960 --> 03:48.040
You're the oldest.

03:49.200 --> 03:50.400
You speak 'em for me.

03:59.760 --> 04:02.720
[Arthur] I'm sorry, brother.
I can't do it.

04:04.040 --> 04:05.280
[weeping]

04:21.519 --> 04:22.519
[sighs]

04:33.840 --> 04:35.920
We could have afforded a golden carriage.

04:40.800 --> 04:42.400
She deserved a golden carriage.

04:47.480 --> 04:49.720
But we didn't
afford ourselves that luxury…

04:53.320 --> 04:54.920
because gold doesn't work.

05:00.960 --> 05:03.280
That was the last lesson
that Ruby taught us.

05:19.000 --> 05:24.000
This place was her favourite place
in the whole world.

05:24.080 --> 05:25.080
And she used to say,

05:26.800 --> 05:27.880
"Dad…

05:30.960 --> 05:33.120
you never know
what's gonna come down the river."

05:35.440 --> 05:36.400
And it's true.

05:38.920 --> 05:40.200
'Cause little Ruby's fate

05:41.320 --> 05:43.120
came a thousand miles too soon.

05:47.760 --> 05:51.720
But in her name
and in her memory, things will change.

05:52.240 --> 05:53.120
[sniffles]

05:55.600 --> 05:57.920
And whatever comes down
that river from now on,

05:58.520 --> 05:59.800
we will make good…

06:03.640 --> 06:05.880
We will make peaceful and honest and good,

06:05.960 --> 06:08.240
and send it on down the river
better than it was.

06:08.320 --> 06:09.960
In her memory, we will do this.

06:16.480 --> 06:17.360
[sniffles]

06:18.760 --> 06:19.840
But for now,

06:20.880 --> 06:21.960
we send her on

06:23.480 --> 06:24.880
to wherever it is you go.

06:27.080 --> 06:29.200
In the hope
that if there is a destination…

06:31.880 --> 06:33.240
…that it's a yard like this.

06:34.160 --> 06:37.680
With horses and boats for her to play on.

06:49.960 --> 06:51.640
[sighs] Tom.

06:52.760 --> 06:54.280
-I've got the petrol.
-[sighs]

06:55.800 --> 06:57.120
Who will light the flame?

07:02.600 --> 07:03.600
Jeremiah.

07:10.360 --> 07:12.960
Jeremiah, you made her laugh.

07:14.080 --> 07:15.240
You light the flame.

07:15.320 --> 07:17.560
No! No!

07:17.640 --> 07:19.480
-Lizzie.
-[Lizzie] No!

07:19.560 --> 07:21.800
You won't burn her! No!

07:21.880 --> 07:23.120
Lizzie. [shushes]

07:23.920 --> 07:25.280
[Lizzie sobbing]

07:26.880 --> 07:31.080
-I just want to see my baby.
-We'll go and see her together. Come on.

07:31.160 --> 07:33.600
-Yeah. Yeah.
-We'll go and see her together.

07:36.280 --> 07:37.240
[sniffles]

07:40.000 --> 07:40.840
[exhales]

07:45.560 --> 07:46.560
Oh, my baby.

08:07.040 --> 08:09.080
The devils who did this will pay, Ruby.

08:13.240 --> 08:14.760
Tommy, what do you mean?

08:18.320 --> 08:19.440
What do you mean?

08:21.200 --> 08:22.120
Where're you going?

09:05.200 --> 09:06.160
[inaudible]

09:06.240 --> 09:07.600
[dramatic music playing]

09:25.000 --> 09:26.200
[inaudible]

09:54.680 --> 09:55.720
[birds chirping]

10:04.720 --> 10:06.040
[vehicle approaching]

10:11.880 --> 10:12.800
[door opens]

10:14.040 --> 10:14.880
[door closes]

10:14.960 --> 10:15.960
Riley.

10:16.760 --> 10:18.240
I think the police are here.

10:20.440 --> 10:21.720
[Tommy] Evadne Barwell?

10:23.320 --> 10:24.160
Yeah.

10:24.680 --> 10:25.680
Who's asking?

10:26.960 --> 10:28.960
[Tommy] I'm here on behalf
of the blue sapphire.

10:29.040 --> 10:29.960
[gunshots firing]

10:30.920 --> 10:31.840
[people shrieking]

10:39.440 --> 10:41.440
[woman] Don't shoot. There are babies!

10:41.520 --> 10:42.920
Go! Come on.

10:43.000 --> 10:44.080
[baby crying]

10:44.160 --> 10:45.680
[woman] We have to go. Come on!

10:45.760 --> 10:47.120
[Tommy breathing heavily]

10:50.960 --> 10:53.200
["Lullaby For Cain" playing]

11:03.040 --> 11:06.600
♪ From the silence ♪

11:06.680 --> 11:10.000
♪ From the night ♪

11:10.080 --> 11:17.040
♪ Comes a distant lullaby ♪

11:18.800 --> 11:22.840
♪ Cry, remember that first cry ♪

11:22.920 --> 11:26.360
♪ Your brother standing by ♪

11:26.440 --> 11:28.160
♪ And lot… ♪

11:28.240 --> 11:29.520
[grunting]

11:29.600 --> 11:32.920
♪ Of loved ♪

11:33.440 --> 11:39.960
♪ Beloved sons of mine ♪

11:42.920 --> 11:48.400
♪ Sing a lullaby ♪

11:50.480 --> 11:56.080
♪ Mother is close by ♪

11:57.280 --> 12:00.200
♪ Innocent eyes ♪

12:00.680 --> 12:05.680
♪ Such innocent eyes ♪

12:07.240 --> 12:08.120
[groans]

12:08.200 --> 12:13.600
♪ Envy stole your brother's life ♪

12:14.080 --> 12:15.080
♪ Came home… ♪

12:15.160 --> 12:16.120
[sobbing]

12:16.200 --> 12:17.240
♪ Murdered ♪

12:17.720 --> 12:21.280
♪ Piece of mind ♪

12:25.320 --> 12:26.440
[sobs]

12:28.360 --> 12:34.600
♪ Left you nightmares on the pillow ♪

12:44.680 --> 12:46.160
[engine running]

12:53.080 --> 12:54.440
[engine stops]

12:55.760 --> 12:57.040
[sighs deeply]

13:06.360 --> 13:07.240
[door closes]

13:11.600 --> 13:12.600
Gold dust.

13:13.600 --> 13:15.360
Our business is done, Esme.

13:15.440 --> 13:16.880
Get out of the car.

13:16.960 --> 13:18.280
[Esme] Not quite done, Tommy.

13:19.600 --> 13:21.240
Thought this'd be a good time.

13:21.800 --> 13:23.440
In fact, it's the perfect time.

13:24.560 --> 13:26.360
Some business is still unfinished.

13:28.280 --> 13:31.040
Christians say, "The Lord gives,
the Lord takes away."

13:31.960 --> 13:33.240
Our spirits are the same.

13:34.240 --> 13:36.160
Spirits just took away your child.

13:36.240 --> 13:38.240
-Get out of the car, Esme.
-[engine starts]

13:38.320 --> 13:41.040
The same spirits want to
give you a different child, Tommy.

13:41.840 --> 13:43.280
[sighs] What child?

13:44.520 --> 13:45.680
[engine stops]

13:45.760 --> 13:46.840
A daughter lost,

13:48.320 --> 13:49.440
a son found.

13:52.400 --> 13:55.000
Before you went to France
a long time ago, at Appleby Fair,

13:55.680 --> 13:56.800
you slept with a girl.

13:57.440 --> 13:58.640
Her name was Zelda.

13:59.400 --> 14:00.360
I met her.

14:01.560 --> 14:05.240
She said you slept together
under a hazel tree in May 1914.

14:07.000 --> 14:10.800
When she fell pregnant
her father threatened to kill you.

14:11.680 --> 14:14.560
But you'd already joined the army
and gone away to France.

14:18.080 --> 14:21.000
You remember the girl
and the hazel tree, don't you, Tommy?

14:24.880 --> 14:27.720
Whoever the boy is, Esme…

14:28.800 --> 14:30.440
Whoever he is, our business is done here.

14:30.520 --> 14:34.120
I brought you to this camp for a reason.
And I brought him as well.

14:35.280 --> 14:36.240
He is yours.

14:37.600 --> 14:39.120
A boy born with hazel eyes.

14:40.400 --> 14:41.840
He calls himself Duke.

14:43.880 --> 14:46.360
His mother is dead. He's a thief.

14:47.040 --> 14:48.160
He works the fairground,

14:48.240 --> 14:51.520
but he says he wants more to life
than big wheels and carousels.

14:55.320 --> 14:58.000
If the losing of Ruby's
left a hole in your heart,

14:59.360 --> 15:00.520
I'll send him to you.

15:02.800 --> 15:04.680
If you give me a bit more gold.

15:06.400 --> 15:12.280
I'll tell him Tommy Shelby can offer a man
far more than big wheels and carousels.

15:12.360 --> 15:13.360
[exhales]

15:14.640 --> 15:16.400
Is our business done or not, Tommy?

15:44.320 --> 15:45.880
[Lizzie] I know where you went.

15:51.080 --> 15:52.080
[exhales]

16:00.160 --> 16:02.800
I'll spend more hours working
in the Commons with Mr Churchill.

16:02.880 --> 16:04.000
His fight is my fight.

16:04.080 --> 16:07.280
I sat like a stone and thought about you
killing someone in her name.

16:07.360 --> 16:09.680
The Shelby institutions will be expanded.

16:11.360 --> 16:14.320
I will set up a fund to research
the causes and cures of consumption.

16:14.400 --> 16:16.360
Did the woman you killed have children?

16:16.440 --> 16:18.480
Ten thousand children
die every year, Lizzie.

16:18.560 --> 16:19.440
Go to bed, Tommy.

16:19.520 --> 16:21.080
I've been reading about new research.

16:21.160 --> 16:23.680
-Stop and close your fucking eyes.
-I will not…

16:23.760 --> 16:25.040
I will not stop!

16:25.120 --> 16:27.640
What is this "good" that you will become?!

16:30.400 --> 16:31.360
[exhales]

16:38.160 --> 16:39.200
I killed a woman.

16:40.920 --> 16:42.680
I killed a woman and three men.

16:42.760 --> 16:46.640
And their bodies will be thrown
aboard the boat like all the other bodies.

16:46.720 --> 16:49.720
But I am stepping off that boat
and onto another boat.

16:51.280 --> 16:52.360
Do you understand?!

16:55.560 --> 16:56.480
Yeah.

17:08.520 --> 17:10.599
The doctor from the sanatorium called

17:10.680 --> 17:13.160
and said that he needs
to speak with you urgently.

17:14.880 --> 17:17.359
But I think you're now
beyond the help of doctors.

17:17.440 --> 17:18.280
Lizzie…

17:19.160 --> 17:20.480
[Lizzie breathing heavily]

17:21.560 --> 17:23.240
Frances said Arthur's here.

17:24.760 --> 17:25.680
[door slams]

17:47.720 --> 17:48.560
[switch flicks]

17:56.080 --> 17:57.000
[Arthur] Tommy?

17:59.000 --> 18:00.680
-Tom?
-[Tommy] Yeah, it's me.

18:02.080 --> 18:03.080
[Arthur] Ah, fuck.

18:21.520 --> 18:22.640
[Tommy exhales]

18:22.720 --> 18:24.400
Arthur, give me a light, will you?

18:25.560 --> 18:26.720
I can't find my lighter.

18:28.960 --> 18:29.800
[exhales]

18:31.560 --> 18:33.080
[sniffs]

18:39.720 --> 18:42.200
Sorry I didn't speak at the wagon, Tom.

18:52.160 --> 18:53.280
Don't be sorry.

18:56.800 --> 18:58.040
What are you doing here?

19:01.120 --> 19:03.760
Waiting for this fucking cup to fill up.

19:08.080 --> 19:09.560
Nearly empty, this barrel.

19:10.040 --> 19:11.200
[scoffs]

19:11.280 --> 19:13.160
Plenty of barrels, Arthur.

19:14.560 --> 19:15.760
Start another barrel.

19:16.760 --> 19:19.320
I thought maybe
they were all full of fucking blood.

19:19.400 --> 19:20.400
[breathes deeply]

19:23.240 --> 19:24.400
The junk, Tom.

19:26.680 --> 19:28.160
Fucks up your mind.

19:32.840 --> 19:33.960
You know, Arthur,

19:36.640 --> 19:38.280
you was already fucked up.

19:38.840 --> 19:39.760
[exhales]

19:40.680 --> 19:43.080
[Tommy] You was fucked up
since you was a kid.

19:45.560 --> 19:46.520
This is my theory.

19:48.840 --> 19:49.680
[clicks tongue]

19:50.840 --> 19:53.240
It's from that time I gave you a beating,

19:53.320 --> 19:55.200
when you was 12 and I was nine.

19:56.560 --> 19:58.360
We were fighting over cigarettes.

20:01.280 --> 20:05.360
Maybe while I had you down on the ground,

20:06.480 --> 20:08.400
I gave you one too many to the head.

20:09.120 --> 20:10.960
It was a draw, though, Tom.

20:11.480 --> 20:12.480
Nah.

20:14.120 --> 20:15.200
I beat you.

20:16.320 --> 20:17.480
I had you pinned.

20:18.040 --> 20:19.240
You actually didn't.

20:20.720 --> 20:21.600
[chuckles softly]

20:21.680 --> 20:22.960
We both agreed.

20:23.040 --> 20:25.320
You're so fucked,
you can't remember, brother.

20:27.520 --> 20:28.440
I do.

20:28.800 --> 20:30.760
I do remember these little things.

20:31.280 --> 20:32.400
[Tommy] I know you do.

20:33.720 --> 20:34.840
So do I.

20:36.080 --> 20:37.960
The fog and the gas is clearing, eh?

20:50.160 --> 20:51.080
[coughs]

21:10.760 --> 21:11.640
[lighter clicks]

21:29.960 --> 21:32.080
Your cup's nearly full, pass it here.

21:36.720 --> 21:37.800
But, Tommy…

21:38.440 --> 21:39.280
[exhales]

21:40.920 --> 21:42.520
You don't drink this stuff any more.

21:43.400 --> 21:44.240
Eh?

21:45.120 --> 21:46.720
You don't drink no more, Tom.

22:08.840 --> 22:09.680
[clicks tongue]

22:10.720 --> 22:12.440
Hell, when Polly was gone, Arthur,

22:14.240 --> 22:16.240
I thought I could just march and march.

22:17.640 --> 22:19.440
I just kept up that fucking left-right,

22:19.520 --> 22:22.280
left-right, left-right,
left-right fucking rhythm.

22:23.360 --> 22:24.760
I'd never have to stop.

22:27.360 --> 22:28.600
Then Ruby went…

22:33.000 --> 22:34.680
and I stumbled and crashed.

22:40.240 --> 22:41.520
Now here I am…

22:43.640 --> 22:44.920
sat on my arse,

22:46.240 --> 22:47.280
on the ground,

22:48.400 --> 22:50.400
like a fucking tunneller…

22:52.720 --> 22:54.680
with my old comrade Arthur.

22:54.760 --> 22:55.640
[exhales sharply]

22:55.720 --> 22:56.680
Yeah.

22:59.600 --> 23:01.200
Remember The January, Arthur?

23:04.120 --> 23:06.960
-The family boat?
-Yeah.

23:07.040 --> 23:10.920
A whole family living on something
the size of ten of these fucking barrels.

23:11.800 --> 23:12.640
Hmm.

23:14.840 --> 23:16.200
Remember that night

23:16.960 --> 23:18.160
at Tile Cross?

23:19.000 --> 23:21.440
Sixteen of us sleeping on the boat.

23:21.520 --> 23:22.600
The coppers come.

23:23.800 --> 23:25.200
We all swim like rats.

23:26.280 --> 23:27.480
Except for Arthur.

23:28.640 --> 23:29.840
Arthur holds them off

23:30.440 --> 23:32.960
with a boat hook, all on his own.

23:34.800 --> 23:35.880
And I remember,

23:37.280 --> 23:39.800
I climbed back up on the lock
and I looked back,

23:39.880 --> 23:42.560
and I saw you
waving that fucking boat hook

23:42.640 --> 23:43.760
in the coppers' faces…

23:43.840 --> 23:44.760
[chuckles]

23:45.680 --> 23:46.680
…on your own.

23:48.360 --> 23:49.560
That's when I realised…

23:51.800 --> 23:53.280
when I had you on the ground,

23:54.400 --> 23:55.800
all them years ago,

23:56.800 --> 23:58.160
it's 'cause you let me win.

23:58.240 --> 23:59.080
[Arthur laughs]

24:02.240 --> 24:03.600
You wanted me to win.

24:07.640 --> 24:09.440
You've wanted me to win ever since.

24:12.160 --> 24:13.680
What chance do I have if you…

24:15.840 --> 24:17.240
start doing that again?

24:18.000 --> 24:18.960
Huh?

24:20.760 --> 24:21.800
You'll stop.

24:22.840 --> 24:25.040
You'll stop
'cause the family needs you to.

24:25.680 --> 24:26.560
[exhales]

24:27.480 --> 24:29.920
It's like that long tunnel
on the Dudley stretch.

24:31.000 --> 24:36.400
Remember Dudley Canal, line number one,
3,172 yards of fucking pitch blackness?

24:36.480 --> 24:38.320
-And rats swimming?
-Yeah.

24:38.400 --> 24:41.880
And then we come round the corner
and there'd be a shaft of light,

24:43.040 --> 24:44.120
and then we'd know.

24:44.920 --> 24:45.760
Yeah.

24:45.840 --> 24:48.600
And then, you and me, we'd both know
it was nearly done.

24:51.680 --> 24:53.320
That's where we are now, Arthur.

24:55.440 --> 24:57.000
Just a few more yards to go.

24:59.640 --> 25:01.160
And you will change your ways.

25:04.760 --> 25:06.480
And I'll change the fucking world.

25:07.360 --> 25:09.360
["Stone Towers" playing]

25:19.680 --> 25:23.160
♪ Like a slumber ♪

25:23.240 --> 25:26.560
♪ In the moss ♪

25:26.640 --> 25:29.680
♪ I could display ♪

25:29.760 --> 25:32.680
♪ In the dark ♪

25:33.520 --> 25:36.000
♪ I have loved you ♪

25:36.920 --> 25:39.720
♪ From the start ♪

25:39.800 --> 25:41.920
♪ But there's cold veneer ♪

25:42.000 --> 25:45.120
♪ Near the cloud of you ♪

25:47.040 --> 25:49.480
♪ Of you ♪

26:01.320 --> 26:04.120
♪ Sit on back in thrones of blue ♪

26:04.600 --> 26:07.560
♪ And inlay black, so righteous you ♪

26:08.040 --> 26:10.640
♪ Bear cold decree ♪

26:11.120 --> 26:12.840
♪ It's dead to me ♪

26:14.840 --> 26:17.720
♪ Sit on through
While your mistakes loom ♪

26:17.800 --> 26:21.080
♪ You're stone-dead blind
And it's drowning all ♪

26:21.560 --> 26:24.080
♪ Your company… ♪

26:24.160 --> 26:26.440
We assumed, at this late hour,
you'd have had dinner.

26:26.520 --> 26:28.680
There are drinks
and sandwiches if you want.

26:29.360 --> 26:30.520
We're not here to eat.

26:31.160 --> 26:33.200
Mr Shelby will be down shortly.

26:33.280 --> 26:37.320
Please tell Mr Shelby on behalf of us all
that changing the world can wait.

26:37.400 --> 26:38.640
[man] He doesn't want to wait.

26:39.160 --> 26:40.160
There is champagne.

26:40.720 --> 26:41.680
Oh, goodie.

26:52.720 --> 26:53.680
Charles?

26:56.320 --> 26:57.520
I heard cars.

26:58.440 --> 26:59.360
[door opens]

27:02.240 --> 27:04.120
-[Frances] Mr Shelby, the guests are--
-I know.

27:06.360 --> 27:09.800
Dad, there's a Bentley and a Rolls Royce.

27:12.840 --> 27:13.800
Yeah.

27:15.960 --> 27:17.080
Go to bed, Charles.

27:25.000 --> 27:26.360
I can't sleep.

27:30.320 --> 27:32.080
I see her when I shut my eyes.

27:33.920 --> 27:35.000
Go to your mum.

27:35.840 --> 27:37.120
She'll be awake.

27:38.000 --> 27:40.600
-She holds on to me.
-[Tommy] Let her hold on to you.

27:42.880 --> 27:43.960
Hear me?

27:44.760 --> 27:46.280
Always let her hold on to you.

27:47.520 --> 27:48.400
Go on.

27:53.400 --> 27:55.920
[Frances] Mr Shelby, the guests said
they would understand--

27:56.000 --> 27:58.320
-Have you served them drinks?
-[Frances] Yes.

27:58.400 --> 27:59.280
Yeah.

28:12.280 --> 28:13.360
I'm okay, Frances.

28:18.960 --> 28:23.320
The agenda is in my head.
The agenda is in my head.

28:25.040 --> 28:26.080
I'm okay.

28:27.760 --> 28:28.880
Do I look okay?

28:32.640 --> 28:34.880
If someone touches you, you won't shatter.

28:37.400 --> 28:38.520
Sing it.

28:39.560 --> 28:41.120
Sing it. I love that song.

28:41.600 --> 28:42.440
I…

28:42.520 --> 28:45.760
I can't be singing rebel songs
in a house in grief and mourning.

28:45.840 --> 28:47.280
Sing it to me softly.

28:47.880 --> 28:49.040
Breaks my heart.

28:50.680 --> 28:52.040
Don't look at him, he's English.

28:52.560 --> 28:53.680
He can block his ears.

28:57.560 --> 29:01.920
Darling, should she sing
her rebel IRA song while we wait?

29:02.560 --> 29:04.160
Or would that be inappropriate?

29:05.640 --> 29:06.480
[lighter clicks]

29:06.960 --> 29:10.400
[sniffs] You know, I went to a meeting
of similar intent to this in Berlin.

29:11.560 --> 29:13.640
Attended by the chancellor himself.

29:14.360 --> 29:16.320
And Göring, and Himmler.

29:18.120 --> 29:19.640
It lasted until the sun came up.

29:20.800 --> 29:24.200
We spoke about the future
of the world in a serious way.

29:26.240 --> 29:28.120
When the first rays of light
entered the room,

29:28.200 --> 29:31.280
we all stood and stared at it
as if it were the world to come.

29:33.000 --> 29:35.400
There was no singing, no giggling.

29:38.560 --> 29:42.160
And when breakfast was served
on the terrace overlooking the mountains,

29:42.240 --> 29:43.720
they brought up some Jews.

29:45.880 --> 29:48.720
And while we ate our eggs,
they were forced to eat grass.

29:50.600 --> 29:53.560
And we watched as we sipped our coffee.

29:59.520 --> 30:01.920
We should all remember
this is serious business.

30:10.320 --> 30:12.720
[Mosley clicks tongue] Well, Diana…

30:15.000 --> 30:17.480
Now look what you've done.
You've killed the mood.

30:18.200 --> 30:19.240
[chuckles]

30:22.880 --> 30:26.200
Let her sing her fucking song
to raise our spirits. Go on, please.

30:36.120 --> 30:40.560
♪ In a neat little town
They call Belfast ♪

30:40.640 --> 30:44.520
♪ Apprentice to trade I was bound ♪

30:44.600 --> 30:48.880
♪ And many an hours sweet happiness ♪

30:48.960 --> 30:52.120
♪ Have I spent in that neat little town ♪

30:52.880 --> 30:56.960
♪ A sad misfortune came over me… ♪

31:08.360 --> 31:10.360
["Blackbird" playing]

31:11.720 --> 31:13.840
♪ Blackbird ♪

31:14.560 --> 31:16.840
♪ Sit on my shoulder ♪

31:16.920 --> 31:18.720
♪ And tell me a song… ♪

31:18.800 --> 31:19.840
[chuckles]

31:19.920 --> 31:20.960
Did it break?

31:21.560 --> 31:23.240
-We'll fix it for you.
-[glass shatters]

31:23.320 --> 31:25.040
♪ When I cry ♪

31:26.200 --> 31:28.600
♪ Do you hear in colour ♪

31:28.680 --> 31:31.200
♪ Or black and white, bird? ♪

31:31.280 --> 31:32.360
[indistinct shouting]

31:35.320 --> 31:37.440
♪ The morning is new ♪

31:37.520 --> 31:40.280
♪ But the feeling is old ♪

31:42.480 --> 31:46.720
♪ Intervene, blackbird
And shorten the road ♪

31:51.600 --> 31:56.760
♪ Blackbird, the way I imagined ♪

31:56.840 --> 31:58.640
♪ Love was wrong ♪

32:03.320 --> 32:05.080
♪ I've come ♪

32:05.680 --> 32:11.200
♪ To love him
Like I couldn't fathom, blackbird ♪

32:14.600 --> 32:15.600
[inaudible]

32:15.680 --> 32:17.120
♪ Tap away ♪

32:17.200 --> 32:18.560
[inaudible]

32:18.680 --> 32:20.040
♪ I fear and I long ♪

32:22.080 --> 32:24.160
♪ Intervene, Blackbird… ♪

32:24.240 --> 32:25.240
[inaudible]

32:25.320 --> 32:26.320
♪ Shorten the road ♪

32:43.040 --> 32:43.960
[gunshot fires]

32:50.920 --> 32:53.040
♪ Blackbird ♪

32:53.120 --> 32:57.720
♪ Slip into my slumber
And show me a song ♪

33:02.600 --> 33:04.120
♪ When I dream ♪

33:05.040 --> 33:07.720
♪ Do you see in colour ♪

33:07.800 --> 33:10.800
♪ Or at all, bird? ♪

33:14.400 --> 33:19.920
♪ The picture is peaceful
But I dream alone ♪

33:20.000 --> 33:21.280
[horse trotting]

33:21.800 --> 33:23.880
♪ Intervene, blackbird ♪

33:23.960 --> 33:25.960
♪ And shorten the road ♪

33:38.760 --> 33:40.560
She's not here anymore.

33:40.640 --> 33:41.640
[sobbing]

33:52.360 --> 33:56.560
♪ Her eyes they shone like diamonds ♪

33:57.120 --> 33:58.920
♪ I thought her the queen… ♪

33:59.000 --> 34:01.880
-[Mosley] Mr Shelby--
-[Tommy] No, please. No condolences.

34:02.440 --> 34:03.720
Thank you all for coming.

34:05.080 --> 34:08.760
Now let's try and find out how this
new world of ours will look, shall we?

34:15.719 --> 34:19.440
Perhaps, Mr Mosley, we can turn to
what practical things Mr Nelson can do

34:19.520 --> 34:22.520
to further our cause
while he is in the country.

34:22.600 --> 34:25.679
It's me who has the ear
of the president of the United States.

34:26.280 --> 34:28.560
Which is kind of why I'm here, right?

34:29.280 --> 34:33.000
We do indeed have things for you
to whisper into the president's ear.

34:34.639 --> 34:36.159
Tell him we are England.

34:36.679 --> 34:38.600
We are the mood England is in.

34:39.159 --> 34:42.840
And in Ireland,
appeasers to the English abound,

34:43.600 --> 34:49.120
but we represent the true liberated spirit
of the country that populated your own.

34:51.400 --> 34:53.520
I hear about communists in both places.

34:54.440 --> 34:56.360
We are the bulwark against them.

34:57.760 --> 34:59.639
When it comes to the working class,

35:00.600 --> 35:04.840
we could move our people
from republicanism to fascism

35:04.920 --> 35:06.000
with just a nudge.

35:07.360 --> 35:08.280
They trust us.

35:09.760 --> 35:11.640
You ride with hounds, Mr Mosley.

35:12.440 --> 35:13.800
Will you hunt communists?

35:14.880 --> 35:16.960
Oh, my hounds are baying.

35:17.640 --> 35:20.480
Shelby, you run as a socialist.

35:28.200 --> 35:31.960
Mr Shelby has one of the largest
Commons majorities in England.

35:32.960 --> 35:35.120
In the heart of England.

35:36.200 --> 35:38.560
When the time comes,
he'll resign his party whip

35:38.640 --> 35:39.960
and run as an independent.

35:44.600 --> 35:47.680
But underneath, do you truly believe
in the cause, Mr Shelby?

35:59.240 --> 36:00.240
I'm here.

36:00.800 --> 36:03.360
[smacks lips] Mr Nelson,
I'm here four nights…

36:05.480 --> 36:06.320
[sighs]

36:07.880 --> 36:08.720
[scoffs]

36:10.280 --> 36:11.920
Four nights after, and I'm here.

36:14.360 --> 36:17.560
In this room, in this meeting.
I'm here and I'm serious.

36:20.200 --> 36:21.600
Prove it to him.

36:25.800 --> 36:27.600
Prove it, physically.

36:39.560 --> 36:40.720
Perish Judah.

36:49.320 --> 36:50.360
Perish Judah.

36:57.480 --> 36:59.080
That thing is going to get us killed.

37:02.680 --> 37:03.600
Go to bed.

37:05.240 --> 37:08.440
At school, they've stopped talking to me.

37:11.280 --> 37:12.320
[scoffs]

37:12.400 --> 37:14.000
They say the Black rubs off.

37:15.160 --> 37:16.000
[scoffs]

37:17.200 --> 37:18.480
When they come to power,

37:19.200 --> 37:20.480
they'll take her off you.

37:22.080 --> 37:23.800
They're gonna separate us all out.

37:26.000 --> 37:27.360
They'll send her to Africa.

37:29.760 --> 37:30.600
Yeah?

37:31.760 --> 37:33.240
And where will they send you?

37:34.920 --> 37:36.520
Where will they send you, Karl?

37:37.600 --> 37:41.680
You're half Gypsy, so to Egypt maybe?

37:46.920 --> 37:51.120
Something I never told you before
because it wasn't important.

37:52.840 --> 37:54.000
Maybe now it is.

37:55.880 --> 37:57.360
Your dad was Jewish.

37:59.440 --> 38:01.800
He was the son of a tailor in Stechford.

38:02.720 --> 38:06.200
They changed their name to Thorne to stop
the bricks coming through the window.

38:08.880 --> 38:10.640
So where will they send you, Karl?

38:14.040 --> 38:17.560
Mr Nelson, you can
report back to your president

38:17.640 --> 38:21.000
that the aristocracy and the meritocracy
are united in their conviction

38:21.080 --> 38:23.680
that a new order is coming.

38:25.640 --> 38:29.400
Also, Mr Nelson, at present,
our weapons are coming from Germany.

38:30.320 --> 38:32.600
The British are closing
our supply lines down.

38:32.680 --> 38:35.040
We would value a supply from Boston.

38:36.400 --> 38:39.080
[Nelson] Weapons I can give you,
if they're to be used in a good cause.

38:39.160 --> 38:42.360
And while on the subject
of import and export,

38:43.000 --> 38:46.400
Mr Shelby,
in light of our new relationship,

38:46.480 --> 38:50.360
and since you have proven your commitment
in a most extraordinary way,

38:51.400 --> 38:55.720
Boston is now officially open
for the importation of your merchandise.

39:01.800 --> 39:02.720
Good.

39:28.400 --> 39:29.840
[suspenseful music plays]

39:35.000 --> 39:36.480
[music intensifies]

39:43.840 --> 39:46.480
If we have established
what we came here to establish,

39:46.560 --> 39:48.560
perhaps we should all say good night.

39:48.640 --> 39:49.600
[Mosley] Absolutely.

40:01.280 --> 40:02.600
[screaming]

40:11.200 --> 40:12.280
[typewriter clacking]

40:37.560 --> 40:41.040
[Lizzie] That's the same typewriter
you bought me all those years ago.

40:41.960 --> 40:43.840
To help me become more respectable.

40:44.920 --> 40:45.800
Remember?

40:47.760 --> 40:48.760
Yeah.

40:50.040 --> 40:51.560
[typewriter clacking]

40:56.360 --> 40:57.480
[Lizzie] This arrived.

40:58.440 --> 40:59.840
It's from the sanatorium.

41:01.600 --> 41:03.560
I've already paid Ruby's medical bills.

41:04.920 --> 41:06.240
I don't think it's a bill.

41:06.840 --> 41:08.160
It says it's urgent.

41:08.240 --> 41:09.760
From the senior consultant.

41:10.960 --> 41:12.480
[typewriter clacking]

41:29.120 --> 41:30.840
Why didn't you come to bed?

41:36.040 --> 41:37.800
Why didn't you come to bed?

41:37.880 --> 41:39.160
[typing stops]

41:43.600 --> 41:45.880
I'm typing up
my recollection of the meeting.

41:47.400 --> 41:49.480
If I… If I do it straight away,

41:50.640 --> 41:52.320
I can quote people word for word.

41:53.960 --> 41:58.720
The information is more useful
to Mr Churchill if it is word for word.

42:00.400 --> 42:01.560
[typewriter clacking]

42:05.200 --> 42:06.040
[exhales]

42:26.200 --> 42:27.280
I burnt her chair.

42:27.360 --> 42:28.360
[sobbing softly]

42:30.120 --> 42:32.400
The paint on the wood
left a smell in the air.

42:33.840 --> 42:35.000
I didn't open the window.

42:37.560 --> 42:38.720
I quite like the smell.

42:43.400 --> 42:44.720
[sobbing]

43:05.280 --> 43:10.320
[Tommy] Not yet. Not yet.

43:13.280 --> 43:17.440
I have this work to do
'cause now I know that I will change.

43:20.040 --> 43:21.160
That I have to change.

43:23.200 --> 43:25.840
And change for good, Lizzie.

43:31.520 --> 43:32.520
Not just yet.

43:44.680 --> 43:45.600
[typing continues]

43:51.760 --> 43:53.160
[distant telephone ringing]

44:04.520 --> 44:05.480
Hello?

44:09.800 --> 44:10.800
Oh.

44:11.560 --> 44:12.760
[both breathing heavily]

44:24.760 --> 44:26.760
["Do You Love Me?" playing]

44:27.440 --> 44:30.160
♪ She had a heart
Full of love and devotion ♪

44:31.240 --> 44:34.200
♪ She had a mind full
Of tyranny and terror ♪

44:35.280 --> 44:38.520
♪ Well, I try
I do, I really try ♪

44:39.200 --> 44:42.280
♪ But I just err, baby
I do, I error ♪

44:43.000 --> 44:46.560
♪ So come and find me
My darling one ♪

44:46.640 --> 44:49.880
♪ I'm down to the grounds
The very dregs ♪

44:50.440 --> 44:53.440
♪ Here she comes
Blocking the sun ♪

44:53.920 --> 44:57.240
♪ Blood running down
The inside of her legs ♪

44:57.800 --> 45:01.040
♪ The moon in the sky
Is battered and mangled ♪

45:01.120 --> 45:02.800
♪ And the bells in the chapel ♪

45:02.880 --> 45:06.800
♪ Go jingle-jangle
Jingle-jangle ♪

45:06.880 --> 45:09.880
♪ Jingle-jangle
Jingle-jangle ♪

45:09.960 --> 45:13.520
♪ Do you love me? ♪

45:19.120 --> 45:20.200
[banging on door]

45:20.320 --> 45:22.440
♪ Do you love me? ♪

45:25.840 --> 45:27.120
I saw him leave.

45:29.040 --> 45:32.240
He keeps this apartment
expressly for this purpose, doesn't he?

45:32.320 --> 45:33.280
[door closes]

45:34.480 --> 45:36.320
Are you following me, Mr Shelby?

45:37.560 --> 45:38.640
I'm flattered.

45:39.360 --> 45:40.320
But why?

45:41.480 --> 45:42.920
When I do business with someone,

45:43.000 --> 45:45.640
I make it my business
to know their secrets.

45:48.560 --> 45:50.640
Mosley's reputation is no secret.

45:51.480 --> 45:52.680
Not him, you.

45:53.480 --> 45:54.320
[lighter clicks]

45:55.880 --> 45:57.480
How did you know I'd come here?

45:58.360 --> 45:59.560
I know things.

46:00.760 --> 46:02.640
I read people's minds, you know…

46:05.760 --> 46:09.040
Little glances across tables. It's a gift.

46:09.120 --> 46:10.160
The whole family.

46:11.320 --> 46:13.120
Witches and sorcerers.

46:22.440 --> 46:24.040
Your uncle will disown you.

46:25.440 --> 46:27.680
Fucking his business partner
behind his back.

46:27.760 --> 46:28.600
[Gina laughs]

46:29.400 --> 46:30.960
You think he has morals?

46:31.040 --> 46:31.920
He's a Catholic.

46:32.000 --> 46:34.480
Men do what they want,
women do what they are told.

46:36.960 --> 46:38.080
Will you tell Michael?

46:39.680 --> 46:40.840
Michael is family.

46:42.240 --> 46:43.960
We are a family healed.

46:45.920 --> 46:47.560
You have no interest in me

46:48.200 --> 46:49.360
or in Michael.

46:51.280 --> 46:53.920
So why don't you just tell me
what you actually want?

47:02.240 --> 47:03.080
[exhales]

47:05.840 --> 47:09.800
You will be with Mosley
when he's in Berlin.

47:11.160 --> 47:15.120
You'll be in the room when he meets
senior members of the German government.

47:15.200 --> 47:16.920
I want to know what is discussed.

47:18.440 --> 47:20.280
And I want to know what is decided.

47:22.960 --> 47:24.080
And if I lie?

47:26.560 --> 47:27.560
I will know.

47:36.920 --> 47:38.920
You know, Michael thinks you're the Devil.

47:40.560 --> 47:42.560
And I think he might actually be right.

47:44.480 --> 47:46.360
That's the other reason I came here.

47:47.120 --> 47:50.040
What are Michael's real intentions
towards me, Gina?

47:51.080 --> 47:52.600
And if you lie, I will know.

47:58.200 --> 48:02.400
Tommy, he intends to complete the deal.

48:04.200 --> 48:05.640
And then you both walk away.

48:11.680 --> 48:12.600
[chuckles softly]

48:17.840 --> 48:18.720
[door closes]

48:20.440 --> 48:21.440
Fuck.

48:28.320 --> 48:29.200
[pen drops]

48:29.840 --> 48:30.800
[sighs]

49:24.760 --> 49:25.680
[exhales]

49:28.600 --> 49:29.640
[fly buzzes]

49:41.640 --> 49:43.200
[knock on door]

49:43.720 --> 49:44.720
Come.

49:47.360 --> 49:49.160
Mr Shelby, Dr Holford.

49:52.360 --> 49:53.400
Send him in.

50:00.760 --> 50:02.680
You said it had to be in person.

50:03.400 --> 50:04.400
Here I am.

50:06.320 --> 50:07.680
You might want to sit down.

50:13.800 --> 50:14.640
[sighs]

50:15.240 --> 50:18.480
Mr Shelby, I know that you are
still grieving for your daughter,

50:20.040 --> 50:21.720
but I have news that cannot wait.

50:26.880 --> 50:31.840
When you were X-rayed and examined
at the sanatorium, ten days ago,

50:34.280 --> 50:37.160
there was no TB found in your lung.

50:39.680 --> 50:41.800
But I am afraid they found something else.

50:42.880 --> 50:45.160
Something related
to your daughter's illness.

50:49.040 --> 50:51.160
They tried
to speak to you at the hospital,

50:52.040 --> 50:53.560
but you were not cooperating.

50:55.200 --> 50:56.680
After your daughter's death,

50:58.160 --> 51:00.520
you could not be found
to be informed in person.

51:01.800 --> 51:05.080
Eventually, as your personal doctor,
they called me.

51:08.600 --> 51:11.280
I didn't offer you tea.
You look like death. Do you want tea?

51:13.240 --> 51:14.160
No.

51:16.160 --> 51:18.800
At the sanatorium,
they conducted blood tests.

51:20.920 --> 51:24.240
The tests suggest
that the shadow you can see

51:24.320 --> 51:28.160
at the base of your skull is not cancer.

51:29.520 --> 51:30.920
It is tuberculoma.

51:33.400 --> 51:36.960
A tubercular growth
caused by the same bacteria as TB.

51:40.800 --> 51:43.040
You may have picked it up
from your daughter.

51:44.760 --> 51:48.120
Once this disease
enters a household, it can run wild.

51:49.200 --> 51:51.640
It can be transmitted with a simple kiss.

51:55.800 --> 51:58.320
It seems the Shelby household
is no exception.

52:02.520 --> 52:06.440
Mr Shelby, as I say,
I am aware that you are still grieving.

52:07.840 --> 52:10.320
But you must understand
this is very serious.

52:12.640 --> 52:15.680
From the size of the tumour,
expansion must have been rapid.

52:17.160 --> 52:20.920
I have no doubt that you are
already experiencing symptoms.

52:22.640 --> 52:24.560
Have you recently suffered seizures?

52:26.080 --> 52:27.640
Bouts of weakness?

52:28.280 --> 52:31.520
Dissociation? Hallucinations?

52:39.240 --> 52:41.360
-[grunts]
-Why didn't you come and see me?

52:44.160 --> 52:45.520
I have work to do.

52:49.240 --> 52:50.440
Am I a danger to others?

52:52.520 --> 52:53.360
No.

52:54.240 --> 52:56.880
Unlike TB, tuberculoma is not infectious.

52:58.000 --> 53:01.840
Mr Shelby, it is not infectious,

53:01.920 --> 53:06.480
but in your case,
I am afraid it is inoperable.

53:08.320 --> 53:10.120
The growth is in your brainstem.

53:10.200 --> 53:13.880
Any attempt to remove it would result
in trauma and brain haemorrhage.

53:18.640 --> 53:20.360
Whilst you were refusing my calls,

53:20.440 --> 53:23.720
I showed your X-rays to three
of the best surgeons in the country.

53:27.880 --> 53:29.760
They all said they would not operate.

53:31.160 --> 53:32.480
That it would be futile.

53:34.160 --> 53:38.160
Of course, you will want
a second opinion for yourself.

53:39.560 --> 53:42.320
Dr Helen Rutherford at St Thomas'.

53:42.880 --> 53:43.880
She is a friend.

53:48.480 --> 53:49.360
[clears throat]

53:55.360 --> 53:56.320
This…

53:58.680 --> 53:59.920
How bad will it get?

54:06.520 --> 54:07.800
As the tumour grows,

54:08.880 --> 54:12.400
the rate of physical
and mental deterioration will increase.

54:17.120 --> 54:21.040
Eventually, you will need
people around you constantly

54:22.040 --> 54:23.600
who love you very much.

54:27.080 --> 54:28.000
How long?

54:31.880 --> 54:35.000
I understand that you have
defeated many enemies, Mr Shelby.

54:36.280 --> 54:37.520
Now you have a new one.

54:38.560 --> 54:39.560
Inside you.

54:41.240 --> 54:42.560
You cannot defeat it.

54:44.160 --> 54:46.120
But you can keep it at bay for a while.

54:47.000 --> 54:50.920
If you live correctly,
if you are determined, and if you fight--

54:51.000 --> 54:54.800
I asked you a question.
So I want an answer.

54:54.880 --> 54:56.680
I don't want your fucking platitudes.

54:57.760 --> 55:02.160
How long before I need people around me
who love me very much?

55:02.840 --> 55:03.680
[door opens]

55:07.080 --> 55:08.960
-Sorry.
-[Tommy] It's fine, Lizzie.

55:09.040 --> 55:10.840
My accountant here was just leaving.

55:15.480 --> 55:16.440
[clears throat]

55:16.520 --> 55:18.960
I will telephone you
when I get back to London.

55:19.040 --> 55:20.160
No, don't have enough time.

55:20.240 --> 55:22.560
You're an accountant,
give me a fucking number now.

55:24.560 --> 55:25.560
[Holford] One year.

55:26.960 --> 55:28.200
Perhaps 18 months.

55:28.760 --> 55:31.760
[clicks tongue] That's fine.
That's all I need to know.

55:31.840 --> 55:34.720
I will adjust
my finances accordingly. Thank you.

55:37.120 --> 55:39.120
I will write you,
explaining the full implications.

55:39.200 --> 55:40.320
Yep, thank you.

55:44.800 --> 55:45.760
Good day.

55:54.520 --> 55:55.800
Something serious?

55:57.080 --> 55:58.640
No. No, just a…

56:00.000 --> 56:02.240
Just a bill I wasn't expecting, and I…

56:03.680 --> 56:04.800
I'll have to pay it.

56:15.040 --> 56:17.160
Can you give me
a minute on my own, Lizzie?

56:21.160 --> 56:22.120
Yeah.

56:30.960 --> 56:31.800
[door closes]

56:37.920 --> 56:38.920
I'm not a devil.

56:42.360 --> 56:44.000
Just an ordinary, mortal man.

56:50.920 --> 56:53.360
[Polly] There will be a war in this family

56:55.320 --> 56:56.920
and one of you will die.

56:59.800 --> 57:00.640
[Tommy] Polly…

57:02.920 --> 57:05.360
Just give me enough time
to do what I have to do.

57:07.680 --> 57:11.040
[Polly] Kill and kill…
